    "summary": "A single hand-woven specimen strip for a Kente cloth, made of imported European cotton. The warp is primarily of blue, through which along the whole length run two bands of maroon, white, gold and black cotton. At either end of the strip are bands of weft patterns in maroon, gold, green and black, while the middle part of the strip is crossed at regular though wide intervals with two weft bands using a second pair of heddles, with between them a pattern built of discontinuous supplementary weft. The ends form a fringe.",
